NEARS-3639 AC-ANALYTICS finding: `language_changed` event never fires from Settings.

Repro (done twice, both directions, both reproduced the absence):
1. Settings > Language row tapped -> settings_row_tapped {row: language, ...} fires (OK)
2. Sheet opens -> screen_view {screen: language_sheet, source: settings} fires (OK)
3. Tap a DIFFERENT language card (fromBottomSheet:true) -> LanguageCardWidget's onTap
   (language_card_widget.dart, pre-existing, unchanged by this ticket) immediately
   calls localizationController.setLanguage(...) as a live preview -- the WHOLE
   sheet (title/subtitle/Update label) visibly re-renders in the new language
   before Update is ever tapped. Confirmed live: UI actually switched EN<->AR
   both times (screenshots + ui_list dumps below).
4. Tap Update -> sheet closes -> setting_page.dart's
   _manageLanguageFunctionality().then() callback runs:
     final localeBefore = localizationController.locale;   // already the NEW
                                                             // locale, because
                                                             // step 3 already
                                                             // applied it
     localizationController.setLanguage(getCacheLocaleFromSharedPref())...
       .then((_) { if (localizationController.locale != localeBefore) { ... } })
   localeBefore is captured AFTER the live-preview already flipped it, so the
   inequality check is a structural no-op -- language_changed can never fire
   from this call site as written.
5. Result: EN->AR and AR->EN both switch the app language correctly, but NO
   `language_changed` event is emitted either time.

Log excerpt (full raw capture around the AR->EN leg, `adb logcat -v time "flutter:I" "*:S"`):
09-19 23:47:18.035 I/flutter ( 9392): analytics: settings_row_tapped {row: language, screen: settings, section: appearance, position: 1}
09-19 23:47:18.035 I/flutter ( 9392): analytics: screen_view {screen: language_sheet, source: settings}
[... UI genuinely switches back to English (confirmed via ui_list dump), no language_changed line ever appears in the full capture ...]

Evidence: overview screenshots ST3-ST4-language-sheet-arabic-selected-update-enabled.png
(same directory) show the sheet already rendering in Arabic before Update is tapped,
which is the mechanism that races the before/after comparison.
